{
  "_readme": [
    "The @blog post format, and what a sync decides to do with it.",
    "",
    "publishedFieldEdit hands offsets to the editor, which is the renderer's",
    "and counts UTF-16 code units. A case with an emoji in the title is in",
    "here for that reason: a byte offset would land the edit in the wrong",
    "place or split a character.",
    "",
    "The header and field patterns use \\S and \\w, which without the u flag",
    "are ASCII - so the accented cases say what actually happens rather than",
    "what a Unicode-aware regex would.",
    "",
    "planSync sorts filenames, and Array.prototype.sort with no comparator",
    "orders by UTF-16 code unit - which puts A.md before a.md.",
    "",
    "Run: pnpm run test (TypeScript) and cargo test (Rust). Both read this."
  ],
